if you're organizing an event or run a  local group then the chairman of  rochester district council wants to hear  from you  councillor simon smith was elected by  his fellow councillors to be the  chairman of rochford district council in  may  and since then he has been on a  whistle-stop tour of the district  visiting events and local groups  he said  being chairman of the council is hard  work it keeps you very busy but it's so  enjoyable it's a real privilege i have  already met so many people who really do  help  create the wonderful community that is  the rockford district  and i'm looking forward to meeting many  more people during my year in office  if you're organizing an event and you'd  like me to attend i'd be more than happy  to try to come along  councillor smith represents the rayleigh  white house award on the district  council and has been a councillor for 11  years  he has lived in the rochford district  since 1990  and has also served on rayleigh town  council  the chairman recently announced his  engagement and as a father to stuart 22  and sarah 17.  he has worked as a teacher at swain park  school in raleigh since it formerly  opened opened in 1997  and prior to that when it was the swain  school  during his year in office the chairman  will be raising money for several local  charities and is set to host lots of  events  so if you would like the chairman to  attend an event you're organizing or  visit a group or organization that  you're part of  please get in touch with julia mitchell  the civic officer  you can call her on zero one seven zero  two  three one eight one double four or email  her at  julia.mitchell at  rochford.gov dot uk  uk  welcome back to side two  being chairman of the council is a busy  job as councillor smith visits a host of  events and organizations across the  district  already this year the chairman has  attended more than 50 events as well as  raising money for local charities across  rochester district  one of the highlights of the chairman's  year is his civic reception which took  place in july in the gardens of the  council offices in south street  councillor smith welcomed a host of  local community groups and organizations  to the reception  it gave him the opportunity to thank  those who contribute their time and  effort to the local community as well as  raise funds for his chosen charities  more than a hundred guests enjoyed  first-rate refreshments to the sounds of  beautiful background music performed by  an instrumental ensemble from the essex  concert orchestra  later on in the afternoon guests were  entertained with music from films and  shows by the swain park school choir  a return by last year's highly praised  young caterers ensured a mouth-watering  spread for guests  the menu was prepared by pupils from the  king edmund school who were invited to  provide the catering for the occasion as  part of their study for the b tech  national award in hospitality  the chairman is hosting plenty more  events during this his year in office  including  eyes front a veterans afternoon show  starring arla sinclair and filmmaker  patrick king  this will be at the swain park school  sir walter rally drive rayleigh essex  ss6 9bz  it'll be held on sunday the 23rd of  october at 2pm  and you can contact julia mitchell  on zero one seven zero two  three one eight one four four  or  julia.mitchell  rochford.gov dot uk  over the last 18 months rochford  district council has been part of a  project with other south essex local  authorities to help businesses access  advice and funding to lower their carbon  emissions  the low carbon business program helps  small and medium enterprises known as  smes in south essex reduce their running  costs by cutting carbon  many smes have already received help and  support and esw chartered accountants in  rayleigh is just one  esw chartered accountants is a young and  dynamic firm which has enjoyed rapid  growth since the practice was  established in 1996.  they were introduced to the low carbon  business programme through a rayleigh  and district chamber of trade meeting  their existing boiler was old and  inefficient and esw hoped they could  replace it  following a visit from the low carbon  business program who explained they  could apply for a grant and how the  process would work esw chartered  accountants decided to go ahead with  replacing the boiler  audit and accountancy manager amy woods  said the assistance provided by the  low-carbon business team made the  application process very straightforward  a small grant of 880 pound funded by the  european regional development fund was  awarded to purchase a new a-rated boiler  which is 90 efficient to replace their  existing approximately 70 efficient  boiler  the boiler replacement should save the  business 253 pounds per annum  esw are one of the many businesses both  in the rocha district and across south  essex that have been helped by the  program  keeping the running costs of your  business as low as possible is crucial  at the moment  we've all seen our energy bills and the  cost of materials increase but it's  often difficult to know where savings  can be made and to decide whether an  investment is worthwhile  this is precisely where the low carbon  business program can help  rob robinson business energy advisor for  the low carbon business program has  visited hundreds of small and medium  enterprises across south essex  he said quite often all that a business  needs is some impartial advice  there are plenty of things that can be  done with little or no investment and in  many cases it helps to have someone  question why you do something or to  highlight the costs attached  if a business wants some advice all they  need to do is contact us and arrange a  convenient time for me to visit  we are fully funded by the european  regional development fund so there's no  cost to the business no commission is  taken and there are no hidden agendas  the low carbon business program is  available until december twenty twelve  to find out more or terrain to arrange a  visit call zero one two six eight  seven five eight  four two three or email  info  at low carbon business that's all one  word dot org dot uk  if you want further information about  the program businesses they have helped  or any of their frequent events visit  their website at www dot low carbon  business or oneword again  dot org dot uk  the council is introducing a series of  improvements in the way you pay for  parking across all car parks in the  district during october  we've purchased new pay and display  parking machines that will offer a  variety of payment options and give  motorists better value for money  these are the main changes  payment by credit or debit card  the ticket machines will allow you to  pay using a chip and pin verification  facility the same as when using your  card for any other transaction  waive and pay  the machines will also accept those  debit cards that have a chip fitted  allowing contactless payments  this provides motorists with a speedier  transaction for small payments without  the need to enter a pin number  payment by mobile phone the machines  will display full details explaining how  to pay using your mobile phone  you'll also be able to receive a text  message to remind you that your ticket  is due to expire and allow you to top up  your ticket should you be delayed in  returning to your vehicle  linear charging  this means that if you don't have the  exact coinage and have to overpay for  your chosen tariff you'll receive any  extra paid as time on your ticket  this will be calculated relative to the  next time band and will mean our  customers receive better value for money  following requests from customers and  traders and feedback from our customer  survey last year the council has decided  to reintroduce the half-hour time band  in the past when the half-hour time band  was offered many motorists  underestimated their time required and  incurred penalty charge notices  so the facility to purchase a half-hour  ticket will be reviewed after six months  now the new parking tariff will be this  up to half an hour 40p  up to 1 hour 80p  up to 2 hours 1 pound 40  up to 3 hours 2 pounds  up to 4 hours 2.40  up to 5 hours 3 pounds and all day will  cost you five pounds  the car parks  old ship lane car park in rochford is  restricted to parking for up to two  hours  webster's way and mill hall car parks in  rayleigh are restricted to parking for  up to four hours but season ticket  holders are permitted to use these car  parks  the approach car park at the rear of  raley station offers an all-day ticket  only  all other council owned pay and display  car parks have no parking time  restrictions  annual and quarterly season tickets are  available for all car parks priced 800  pounds and 240 pounds respectively  season tickets for the approach car park  at raley station are 700 pounds and 200  pounds  and don't forget with the continuation  of the council's free parking on  saturday afternoon scheme a play and  display ticket need only be purchased to  cover you up to 1pm  if you arrive after this time you park  free in any of rochford council's pay  and display car parks  the council will continue to offer free  parking on sundays and bank holidays  the council has made a number of  improvements to the parking facilities  in the past few years which have  benefited motorists and traders alike  including ensuring all car parks are  park mark accredited and we will  continue to look for opportunities for  further enhancements  full details are available on the  parking page on our website or by  calling transportation on  01268  798 606 or 798 608
 

